                <pb facs="0828" n="716" sameAs="frus:frus1918/pg716"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.6363/383</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Tampico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Dawson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tampico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-04-15T19:00:00-06:41">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 15, 1918, 7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Referring to my April 14, 6 p.m. Outrages by Government troops continue and
                    foreign and Mexican workers are actually abandoning fields. Attitude of
                    Government troops so sudden and unexpected that strong suspicion exists of
                    German influence at work. Embassy advised.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dawson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d649-a1.xml" xpointer="d649-a1"/>
